model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Every hosted Worker that installs the shared telemetry layer writes each Effect log line, in every event, in its initialization and in the layers built over that layer, as one console.log call whose only argument is Effect's structured object (message, level, timestamp, cause, annotations, spans, fiberId), so the runtime adapter's log store indexes the line's fields, and spans keep the line as an event. With exporters configured the object replaces their JSON-string console sink; remote log export is unchanged. Before a line is formatted, failures in its message, fields, Effect containers, annotations and cause are recorded as telemetry records them: a tagged error by its tag and declared sentence, an untagged Error by its name and the first line of its message with URLs, email addresses, quoted values and long runs containing a digit replaced, anything else as UnrecognizedFailure. An error's other fields, nested causes and stack are not stored. App page failures log their cause and config keys instead of a rendered cause, and a failed source format logs the formatter error, not its message. Lines Alchemy logs outside a Worker's layers, such as a Workflow run's scope close, keep Alchemy's logger."
    }
  }
}
